# Jump To Tag, from the flight map's menu: "Jump to Tag" asks for a "Tag Id:", a number from 0 to
# 65535 as UInt16.TryParse takes one, and sends MAV_CMD_DO_JUMP_TAG with it through doCommand,
# which waits for the vehicle's answer. A tag that is not one is "Invalid Tag. Must be a number
# from 0 to 65535", and the question is asked again, as the C#'s handler calls itself. The C#'s
# menu is on the map, and so is this application's since its map menu was ported (the row under
# the Actions grid that held its entries before is gone).
# `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:6618-6645, GCSViews/FlightData.Designer.cs:2518-2531, 2645-2649`
#
# Needs SITL: tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-jumptotag.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 7

# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click fly-tab-actions
expect fly.tab tabActions
expect fly.page.overflow 0

click map@0.5x0.5:right
expect fly.menu map
click fly-jumptotag
expect fly.prompt Tag Id:
type 70000
click fly-prompt-ok
expect status Invalid Tag. Must be a number from 0 to 65535
expect fly.prompt Tag Id:
expect fly.sent nothing yet

type 5
expect fly.prompt.value 5
click fly-prompt-ok
expect fly.prompt none
expect fly.sent COMMAND_LONG MAV_CMD_DO_JUMP_TAG 5,0,0,0,0,0,0
# SITL answers; with no tag 5 in its mission it refuses, which is Strings.CommandFailed.
expect fly.ack ~ MAV_CMD_DO_JUMP_TAG:
